# slug: ch24-lower-call
# source: chapters/ch24.tex:111
# label: alg:ch24-lower-call
# pseudocode source: chapters/ch24.tex:113
# caption: Lower a call and fix the enclosing frame

REQUIRE call node C with signature S, current frame F
ENSURE ABI-conformant sequence replacing C, updated F
classify each argument of S into registers or stack slots
assign return location: register pair or hidden pointer
spill all live caller-saved registers around C
reserve the outgoing area and establish the ABI stack position and alignment
store stack arguments at their ABI offsets in F
place register arguments with a parallel copy; break copy cycles using a scratch location
verify stack alignment at the call point
emit the call and copy the result to a fresh virtual
restore spilled caller-saved registers
record unwind and debug info for new frame ranges

